The fourteenth pass, on the published PDF last modified 18:19 UTC on 4 November (141 pages, 31 chapters). A change in how I measure: for the figures I used to match the pages against my copy of the chapters of 11:18, which is stale (the online view is waiting on security). This time I took today's chapters from a dry run of the builder, with nothing released, so the figure counts below are firm: 94 figure lines, all found by their caption. The figure numbers in 046 and 050 were measured against the old copy and are not comparable with these; the tails and short pages are measured from the PDF alone and are comparable. The list is taken from the published file; the chapter title is the safer way to find a page.

Tails (a chapter's last page, under a quarter full), emptiest first: page 114 "Principles, and build your own" (3 lines, 7% full); 90 "What did not work" (3 lines, 12%); 27 "Hour one: the empty project" (4 lines, 14%); 120 "The tour, at length" (5 lines, 16%); 51 "Hours four and five: before dawn" (6 lines, 17%); 38 "Roles as a cast you can read" (6 lines, 19%); 137 "Appendix A: every number, and how to rerun it" (9 lines, 23%).

Short pages inside a chapter (under 70% full), emptiest first: 49 "Hours four and five: before dawn" (23%, 6 lines: the emptiest page inside a chapter in the book); 105 "The second factory" (55%, 18 lines); 40 "Hour three: every wake read twice, and the first to be caught" (56%, 24 lines); 84 "Hour nineteen, minute by minute" (57%, 16 lines). Borderline, within three points of 70%: 101 "Sessions end" (67%), 19 "The tour: what a factory made in a day" (69%, a raster figure is on this page) and 92 "How do we contain this" (69%).

Changes in tails and short pages since 050 (the 17:13 file), by chapter. Fixed: tails in "Inventing on principle" and "The words used"; short pages in "What did not work", "The tour, at length", "Hour one" and "A second team, reading cold"; the short page in "The tour: what a factory made in a day" (45% before) is now borderline. New: tails in "What did not work", "The tour, at length", "Hours four and five", "Roles as a cast you can read" and "Appendix A"; short pages in "Hours four and five" (the 23% one) and "How do we contain this" (borderline).

Figures whose caption begins a page after their paragraph (information for the writers, the layout's trade): 16, 13 after a paragraph and 3 after a heading, by chapter with the page of the caption: "Slides as a compromise" 9, 10, 10, 11; "The tour: what a factory made in a day" 16 (after a heading); "Talking through git" 58; "The creator comes back" 68, 70; "The story before the slides, and the objection kept" 72; "Hour nineteen, minute by minute" 85; "How do we contain this" 93, 95; "Sessions end" 102; "Principles, and build your own" 112; "The tour, at length" 117 and 118 (both after a heading). I have not read the page ends of these this time.

What the tool cannot tell: whether a short page is meant, whether the drawing under a caption is on the same page as the caption (it finds the caption, not the drawing), and how a page looks beyond how far its content reaches. Full result: review/anchors/print-check.json.

